{"id": "EUVD-2026-108690", "enisaUuid": "10d74bcf-c464-301f-b30e-051b9030dd44", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nthunderbolt: Keep the domain reference while processing hotplug\n\nWe process hotplug events in a workqueue that may run after the domain\nhas been removed by tb_domain_remove(). For example if user unloads the\ndriver while at the same time plugging  a device router we may have\nscheduled tb_handle_hotplug() to run. Avoid possible UAF in this case by\ntaking the domain reference before scheduling the hotplug handler in\ntb_queue_hotplug().", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06b2e894e640f6a3dbeb536a2d26d72426b26a46", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d991f749a8255ee2ecc6307e2f27354ab631827", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8656465d08ed832e120c9cca4a6d0c8ccb45698", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b61a4ae2ec6a0d363615d01106e0a2d284133a38", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04df2985159e381c88a923fae1bec2f8d0272412", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a87af3b1e3aa2e09d160848daf0c39e765b73de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/138ec65b2c761f065b19d115aed2b8246fc272f5", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98896"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vrr8-45r3-5hwq", "CVE-2026-98896"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "28c4549c-e789-3e35-a55e-17bef2a765e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <138ec65b2c761f065b19d115aed2b8246fc272f5"}, {"id": "2c315033-7134-3276-bd77-b59e216d25c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.1.189"}, {"id": "36121dea-f4c3-3198-80ee-183a787a8aac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "5ca0a405-e1c9-321e-9f67-e9f467b7a5fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name